{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "outDir": "dist"
  },
  // EVERY hand-written TypeScript file in the repo, deliberately — one program,
  // one set of compilerOptions, no second config that can drift.
  //
  // `test/**/*` was ABSENT until 2026-08-29, and its absence is why "tsc clean"
  // was a green wider than it was: `npx tsc --noEmit` checked ~290 colocated
  // `src/**/__tests__` files and skipped all 127 files under `test/`. It cost a
  // real defect — a `StampSpec.pri` widening from `boolean` to a union left
  // three call sites in test/art/composer-buffer.test.ts mistyped, tsc reported
  // clean, and a human found them by reading the file.
  //
  // ONE config rather than a `tsconfig.test.json`: the test files need nothing
  // the src build does not already give them. They import `describe`/`it`/
  // `expect` from 'vitest' explicitly (all 127 do — vitest's `globals: true` is
  // belt-and-braces, not load-bearing), they use no path aliases, and they need
  // no extra `lib`/`types`. So a second config would buy looseness nobody asked
  // for and one more thing to keep in sync. If a test subtree ever DOES need a
  // weaker option, split it out then — never weaken this one to reach green.
  //
  // The root `*.ts` entry picks up vitest.config.ts and electron.vite.config.ts,
  // which nothing checked either. `scripts/` and `scratchpad/` are .mjs and stay
  // out: checking them needs `allowJs`, which is a separate decision.
  "include": ["src/**/*", "test/**/*", "*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
